BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|Sept
  17 - ADAS\, AV\, and AI Meetup|Online
DTSTART:20260917T100000
CATEGORIES:ai,cloud,data,frontend,mobile,security
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nJoin our virtual meetup to hear talks from experts on cutting-edge topics
  across AI\, ML\, and computer vision.\n\n**Time\, Date and Location**\n\n
 Sep 17\, 2026\n9:00 AM - 11:00 AM PST\nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](
 https://voxel51.com/events/adas-av-and-ai-meetup-september-17-2026)**\n\n*
 *AI for Autonomous Driving: From Data to Decisions**\n\nBuilding reliable 
 automated driving systems is as much a data and engineering challenge as a
  modeling one. In this talk\, Tin will share perspectives from his work at
  Porsche AG on applying modern AI methods across the autonomous driving de
 velopment process\, from making sense of large-scale driving data to under
 standing and evaluating how AI-based systems behave on the road. He'll dis
 cuss lessons learned from real-world development\, where today's approache
 s shine\, and where hard problems remain for the ADAS and AV community.\n\
 n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Tin Stribor Sohn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/tin
 -stribor-sohn/) is a PhD Student at Porsche AG and Karlsruhe Institute of 
 Technology in the area of Foundation Models for Scenario Understanding and
  Decision Making in Autonomous Robotics\, Tech Lead at Data Driven Enginee
 ring for Autonomous Driving\, Prior: Master in CS at University of Tuebing
 en with focus on Computer Vision and Deep Learning and co-founder of a sof
 tware company for smart EV charging\n\n**Advancing ADAS and Autonomous Veh
 icle Development with Multimodal Data**\n\nADAS and autonomous vehicle sys
 tems rely on increasingly complex data from cameras\, video\, LiDAR\, rada
 r\, and other sensor streams. In this session\, Murilo will introduce Voxe
 l51 and explore how the latest multimodal capabilities in FiftyOne help te
 ams bring these data sources together to better understand their datasets 
 and model behavior. He’ll discuss how unified workflows for visualizatio
 n\, search\, curation\, and evaluation can help ADAS and AV teams uncover 
 challenging scenarios\, investigate model failures\, and build safer\, mor
 e reliable autonomous systems.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Murilo Gustineli
 ](https://www.linkedin.com/in/murilo-gustineli/) is a Machine Learning Eng
 ineer at Voxel51 working at the intersection of representation learning an
 d computer vision. He holds an M.S. in Computer Science from Georgia Tech\
 , where he co-leads the DS@GT Applied Research & Competitions group\, adva
 ncing machine learning research through competitive challenges and peer-re
 viewed publications.\n\n**From Survey-Grade Maps to Physical AI: Scaling R
 eal-World Data for Training and Simulation**\n\nPhysical AI systems are in
 creasingly constrained not by model architectures\, but by the availabilit
 y of scalable\, high-fidelity real-world data. This talk explores how Dyna
 mic Map Platform transforms survey-grade road assets collected across 1.8 
 million km of roads worldwide into training- and simulation-ready datasets
 \, including point clouds\, imagery\, HD maps\, road surface models\, and 
 3D Gaussian Splatting representations.\n\nWe will discuss why geometric ac
 curacy\, semantic understanding\, and real-world diversity are critical to
  building robust autonomous driving systems. Attendees will learn how real
 -world geospatial data can be structured and scaled for AI training and si
 mulation workflows.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Ryoto Miyake](https://www.l
 inkedin.com/in/ryoto-miyake/) is a Software Engineer at Dynamic Map Platfo
 rm\, where he works on transforming large-scale geospatial data into AI-re
 ady datasets for training\, simulation\, and validation\, such as HD maps 
 and 3D Gaussian Splatting. With a background in transportation engineering
 \, he works closely with automotive manufacturers and industry partners to
  bridge large-scale real-world mapping data with next-generation AI and mo
 bility systems.
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cloud Native Mexico City|Cloud Native CDMX - Beyond Tool Sprawl: D
 ynamic Multi-Cloud Operations|Online
DTSTART:20260917T120000
CATEGORIES:ai,cloud,data,devops,frontend,mobile,security
DESCRIPTION:🚀 Cloud Native CDMX Online! in virtual format!\nWe continue
  building the Cloud Native community in Mexico City with a new session of 
 learning\, networking\, and technology\, this time from the comfort of you
 r home.\n📅 Thursday\, September 17\, 2026\n🕛 12:00 PM (Mexico City\,
  UTC-6) / 6:00 PM (UTC)\n💻 Online event\n🎟️ Completely free admiss
 ion!\nThis session will feature a high-level technical talk:\n🎤 Beyond 
 Tool Sprawl: An Event-Driven Approach to Dynamic Multi-Cloud Operations by
 \nEleni Grosdouli\nLet's be honest we've all felt the pain of waiting for 
 resources\, whether it's a database\, a secret\, or an application. And if
  that wasn't enough\, tool sprawl is a real issue: juggling multiple tools
 \, CLIs\, and workflows to get things done across different environments. 
 But what if teams could create on-demand services across multi-cloud envir
 onments using events\, without adding yet another tool to an already overl
 oaded toolset?\nIn this talk\, Eleni will introduce an intuitive\, event-d
 riven approach for efficient multi-cloud operations. We'll demonstrate how
  Sveltos\, an open-source tool for declarative multi-cloud operations\, en
 ables us to orchestrate on-demand services and resources in a dynamic\, sc
 alable\, and straightforward manner all while adhering to GitOps best prac
 tices.\nDesigned for DevOps engineers\, SREs\, Platform Engineers\, and Cl
 oud Native enthusiasts\, this session will show you how to adopt a dynamic
 \, event-driven approach that simplifies multi-cloud operations and elimin
 ates tool sprawl complexity.\n👩‍💻 About Eleni Grosdouli: DevOps Co
 nsulting Engineer at Cisco Systems\, a DevOps and GitOps expert passionate
  about networking\, security\, and endpoint management. With hands-on expe
 rience across diverse technical domains\, Eleni is a lifelong learner who 
 loves experimenting with cutting-edge technology in her home lab and shari
 ng her discoveries through blog posts. When she's not working on tech proj
 ects\, she channels that same energy into sports she recently joined a loc
 al rugby team. 🏉\nCloud Native CDMX continues to grow with the mission 
 of building a strong\, inclusive\, and passionate technical community arou
 nd the Cloud Native ecosystem in Mexico.\nBe part of the community! 🙌\n
 🚀 ¡Cloud Native CDMX Online! Sexta edición de nuestro capítulo ¡en 
 formato virtual!\nSeguimos construyendo comunidad Cloud Native en Ciudad d
 e México con una nueva sesión de aprendizaje\, networking y tecnología\
 , esta vez desde la comodidad de tu hogar.\n📅 Jueves 17 de Septiembre d
 e 2026\n🕛 12:00 hrs (Ciudad de México\, UTC-6) / 18:00 hrs (UTC)\n💻
  Evento en línea\n🎟️ ¡Entrada completamente gratuita!\nEsta sesión
  contará con una ponencia de alto nivel técnico:\n🎤 Beyond Tool Spraw
 l: An Event-Driven Approach to Dynamic Multi-Cloud Operations by\nEleni Gr
 osdouli\nSeamos honestos: todos hemos sentido la frustración de esperar p
 or recursos\, ya sea una base de datos\, un secreto o una aplicación. Y s
 i eso no fuera suficiente\, el tool sprawl es un problema real: malabarear
  múltiples herramientas\, CLIs y workflows para hacer las cosas en difere
 ntes entornos. Pero\, ¿qué pasaría si los equipos pudieran crear servic
 ios bajo demanda en entornos multi-cloud usando eventos\, sin agregar otra
  herramienta más a un toolset ya sobrecargado?\nEn esta charla\, Eleni pr
 esentará un enfoque intuitivo y event-driven para operaciones multi-cloud
  eficientes. Demostraremos cómo Sveltos\, una herramienta open-source par
 a operaciones multi-cloud declarativas\, nos permite orquestar servicios y
  recursos bajo demanda de manera dinámica\, escalable y directa\, todo mi
 entras se adhiere a las mejores prácticas de GitOps.\nDiseñada para inge
 nieros DevOps\, SREs\, Platform Engineers y entusiastas del ecosistema Clo
 ud Native\, esta sesión te mostrará cómo adoptar un enfoque dinámico y
  event-driven que simplifica las operaciones multi-cloud y elimina la comp
 lejidad del tool sprawl.\n👩‍💻 Sobre Eleni Grosdouli: DevOps Consul
 ting Engineer en Cisco Systems\, experta en DevOps y GitOps con pasión po
 r networking\, seguridad y gestión de endpoints. Con experiencia práctic
 a en diversos dominios técnicos\, Eleni es una aprendiz de por vida que d
 isfruta experimentar con tecnología de vanguardia en su home lab y compar
 tir sus descubrimientos a través de blog posts. Cuando no está trabajand
 o en proyectos tech\, canaliza esa misma energía en el deporte\; reciente
 mente se unió a un equipo local de rugby. 🏉\nCloud Native CDMX sigue c
 reciendo con la misión de construir una comunidad técnica sólida\, incl
 usiva y apasionada por el ecosistema Cloud Native en México.\n¡Sé parte
  de la comunidad! 🙌
LOCATION:Online
X-CRONQUILES-ADDRESS:Online
X-CRONQUILES-COUNTRY:México
X-CRONQUILES-COUNTRY-CODE:MX
END:VEVENT
